<figure class="pg-figure" data-parameter-plans aria-labelledby="pg-parameters-title">
 <figcaption id="pg-parameters-title"><span>Figure 7</span> One parameter, two very different populations</figcaption>
 <div class="pg-stage">
 <div class="pg-selector"><label for="pg-customer">Customer</label><select id="pg-customer" data-customer><option value="common">1001 · common</option><option value="rare">1002 · rare</option></select></div>
 <p class="pg-result" data-population data-live>84,000 matching orders</p>
 <div class="pg-compare">
  <div><b>Custom plan</b><div class="pg-arrow">↓ knows this customer value</div><div class="pg-flow-node"><strong data-custom data-live>Sequential scan</strong><span data-custom-detail data-live>Read orders once; keep the common customer's rows.</span></div></div>
  <div><b>Generic plan</b><div class="pg-arrow">↓ plans for $1</div><div class="pg-flow-node"><strong data-generic data-live>Bitmap heap scan</strong><span data-generic-detail data-live>Use the customer index; fetch many matching heap rows.</span></div></div>
 </div>
 <p data-parameter-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The custom plan sees that 1001 owns most orders. The generic plan uses the same estimate and route for either customer.</p>
 </div>
 <p class="pg-caption">Measured forced custom and generic plans for <code>SELECT order_id, placed_at, status FROM orders WHERE customer_id = $1</code>. This retrieves every matching order; it is separate from the ten-row history query. The selector displays recorded plans, not a live database.</p>
 <details><summary>Both parameter cases, as text</summary><p>Customer 1001 matches 84,000 orders. The custom plan scans the table; the generic plan uses a bitmap heap scan. Customer 1002 matches 36 orders. The custom plan uses an index scan; the generic plan uses a bitmap heap scan. A generic plan estimates the same population whichever customer is supplied.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-parameter-plans]').forEach(root=>{
 root.querySelector('select')!.addEventListener('change',(event)=>{
  const common=(event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value==='common';
  root.querySelector('[data-population]')!.textContent=common?'84,000 matching orders':'36 matching orders';
  root.querySelector('[data-custom]')!.textContent=common?'Sequential scan':'Index scan';
  root.querySelector('[data-custom-detail]')!.textContent=common?"Read orders once; keep the common customer's rows.":'Use the customer index; fetch a few matching heap rows.';
  root.querySelector('[data-generic-detail]')!.textContent=common?'Use the customer index; fetch many matching heap rows.':'Use the customer index; fetch a few matching heap rows.';
  root.querySelector('[data-parameter-explanation]')!.textContent=common?'The custom plan sees that 1001 owns most orders. The generic plan uses the same estimate and route for either customer.':'For 1002, the custom estimate recognises a small population. The generic estimate still describes an average customer; its chosen route happens to fit this rare value.';
 });
 });
</script>
